cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "LLM-elicited beliefs about economic elasticities"
authors:
  - family-names: Ghenis
    given-names: Max
    affiliation: PolicyEngine
repository-code: "https://github.com/PolicyEngine/llm-econ-beliefs"
url: "https://policyengine.org/ai-beliefs"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - large language models
  - economic elasticities
  - belief elicitation
  - taxable income elasticity
  - optimal taxation
abstract: >-
  Elicitation harness, 12,090-run retained main-panel dataset, and paper studying
  the prompt-conditioned response distributions that 31 frontier large
  language models from 10 organizations produce when asked about
  26 economic quantities with 15 successful repeated runs per model-quantity
  cell. All retained main runs are tagged v4; three sign-clarified quantities
  retain two disclosed prompt wordings. Follow-ups, pilots, and archived
  failed attempts are counted separately in results/archive-manifest.json.
